3.6 Admission to membership shall take effect upon payment of the prescribed admission fee and the minimum share capital contribution as determined from time to time by the General Meeting. Upon admission, the society shall be issued a certificate of membership signed by the President and the Secretary, and its name shall be entered in the Register of Members kept by the Secretary.

3.7 The Register of Members shall be maintained in accordance with the Cooperative Societies Law, and shall contain, in respect of each member society:
(a) the name and registration number of the society;
(b) the date of admission;
(c) the address of its registered office;
(d) the names of the society's authorised representatives for the purposes of dealing with the Union;
(e) such other particulars as the Council may from time to time direct.

3.8 The Register of Members shall be open to inspection by any member society, or by any person authorised in writing by a member society, at the Union's head office during normal office hours, upon payment of a nominal fee to be fixed by the Council.

3.9 The rights and privileges of membership shall not be transferable, and no person or society shall be entitled to exercise the rights of membership save the society whose name appears in the Register of Members.

